{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q003_actin_like_atpase_divergence","answer":"SCOPe 2.08 places the catalytic domains of Actin/HSP70, hexokinase, and glycerol kinase in the same superfamily, c.55.1 'Actin-like ATPase domain' (sunid 53067), within fold c.55 (named 'Ribonuclease H-like motif' in this release; that fold name is a historical label and does not imply RNase H activity). They are separate families: Actin/HSP70 is c.55.1.1 (sunid 53068), hexokinase is c.55.1.3 (sunid 53083; mammalian type I hexokinase and glucokinase are under it), and glycerol kinase is c.55.1.4 (sunid 53089).

What this permits: SCOPe's superfamily-level grouping is a claim of common evolutionary origin (homology) for the shared ATP-binding/phosphotransfer core, so the three share an ancestral fold architecture and a nucleotide-binding core. It is a remote-homology relationship. Because the families are distinct, it does not establish close sequence identity, shared substrate, shared mechanism, or shared cellular role. Actin/HSP70 family members act as cytoskeletal and chaperone proteins, hexokinase phosphorylates hexoses, and glycerol kinase phosphorylates glycerol; you should not transfer a function, substrate specificity, regulatory mode, or inhibitor profile from one family to another on the basis of this classification.

Limits: a superfamily-level match is not sufficient for template use for function prediction or docking; use family-specific structures and representatives (for example, one per family) and validate with family-appropriate evidence such as experimental activity assays, substrate-binding data, or residue-level alignment of the catalytic motifs. Sequence-only searches may miss these relationships. The classification is release-specific: these facts are from release 2.08 (stable label 2.08-stable; latest periodic update 2.08-2026-08-16), and I did not verify whether that periodic update changed any of these nodes.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/search?q=Hsp70","/api/v1/search?q=actin","/api/v1/search?q=hexokinase","/api/v1/search?q=glycerol","/api/v1/search?q=actin-like%20ATPase%20domain","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53066","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53067","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53068","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53083","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/53089","pretrained model knowledge of Actin/HSP70, hexokinase, and glycerol kinase biology"]}]}
